        },
        {
          "name": "Son",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "sit"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "Nope. He told his army to fill in the sea. Turn the island into land, and walk right up to the walls.",
      "word_count": 22
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-01",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The island city",
      "start": 52,
      "duration": 14,
      "image": "images/shot-01.png",
      "background": "mapalex",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": "332 BC",
      "narration": "332 BC. Alexander has just beaten the Persian king at Issus, and he's marching down the coast of the Mediterranean. City after city opens its gates to him. All except one: Tyre.",
      "word_count": 32
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-02",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The island city",
      "start": 66,
      "duration": 13,
      "image": "images/shot-02.png",
      "background": "tyresea",
      "camera": "slow pan right",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": "Tyre",
      "narration": "Tyre was one of the richest ports in the world, home of the Phoenician sea traders and of a purple dye so expensive that only kings could wear it.",
      "word_count": 29
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-03",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The island city",
      "start": 79,
      "duration": 16,
      "image": "images/shot-03.png",
      "background": "tyresea",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": "Half a mile out at sea",
      "narration": "And it was built on an island, about half a mile offshore. Its walls rose straight out of the sea. Ancient writers claimed they stood a hundred and fifty feet high on the side facing the land.",
      "word_count": 37
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-04",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The island city",
      "start": 95,
      "duration": 14,
      "image": "images/shot-04.png",
      "background": "tyrewall",
      "camera": "slow pan left",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Tyrian",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Tyrian",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Tyrian",
          "expression": "gentle",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "Without a strong navy, attacking Tyre looked impossible, and the Tyrians knew it. When Alexander asked to enter the city to make a sacrifice at its temple, they told him no.",
      "word_count": 31
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-05",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The island city",
      "start": 109,
      "duration": 11,
      "image": "images/shot-05.png",
      "background": "tyrewall",
      "camera": "quick push in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Tyrian",
          "expression": "angry",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Tyrian",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "Then, when he sent heralds to talk peace, the Tyrians executed them and threw them from the walls, in full view of his army.",
      "word_count": 24
    },
    {
      "id": "why-1",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Why Tyre mattered",
      "start": 120,
      "duration": 14,
      "image": "images/why-1.png",
      "background": "mapalex",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": "The Persian navy",
      "narration": "Here's what most people miss. Alexander could have simply marched past Tyre. But the Persian king still had a powerful navy, and most of its ships came from Phoenician cities like Tyre.",
      "word_count": 32
    },
    {
      "id": "why-2",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Why Tyre mattered",
      "start": 134,
      "duration": 18,
      "image": "images/why-2.png",
      "background": "mapalex",
      "camera": "static",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": "The danger behind him",
      "narration": "If Alexander marched on to Egypt with Tyre still standing, that fleet could sail around behind him, raid Greece, and stir up revolt back home. His logic was simple: take the ports, and the Persian navy has nowhere left to go.",
      "word_count": 41
    },
    {
      "id": "talk-strategy-1",
      "speaker": "son",
      "section": "Why Tyre mattered",
      "start": 152,
      "duration": 6,
      "image": "images/talk-strategy-1.png",
      "background": "tyresea",
      "camera": "static",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Father",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Son",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "Wait, so it wasn't just his ego? He actually had a reason?",
      "word_count": 12
    },
    {
      "id": "talk-strategy-2",
      "speaker": "father",
      "section": "Why Tyre mattered",
      "start": 158,
      "duration": 18,
      "image": "images/talk-strategy-2.png",
      "background": "tyresea",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Father",
          "expression": "determined",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Son",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "A very good one. Other generals looked at Tyre and saw an island. Alexander saw the key to the whole sea. Win the coast, and you beat a navy without ever fighting it on the water. He was thinking two moves ahead.",
      "word_count": 42
    },
    {
      "id": "dream",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Why Tyre mattered",
      "start": 176,
      "duration": 24,
      "image": "images/dream.png",
      "background": "tent",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Alexander",
          "expression": "closed",
          "pose": "sit"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "Plutarch, Life of Alexander",
      "narration": "There was faith involved too. Alexander claimed descent from the hero Heracles, whom the Tyrians worshipped as their god Melqart. One night, he dreamed that Heracles reached out from the walls of Tyre and took his hand. His seer said it meant the city would fall, but only after great labor. He was right on both counts.",
      "word_count": 57
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-06",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "A road across the sea",
      "start": 200,
      "duration": 9,
      "image": "images/shot-06.png",
      "background": "tyresea",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Officer",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Alexander",
          "expression": "determined",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "Alexander didn't scream or storm off. He called in his best engineers and gave an order that left his officers speechless.",
      "word_count": 21
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-07",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "A road across the sea",
      "start": 209,
      "duration": 13,
      "image": "images/shot-07.png",
      "background": "tyresea",
      "camera": "quick push in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Engineer",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Alexander",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "“Build a road to the island.”",
      "narration": "His plan, in plain words: if we can't sail to the island, we'll build a road to it. A causeway of stone and timber, straight across the sea.",
      "word_count": 28
    },
    {
      "id": "talk-beach-1",
      "speaker": "son",
      "section": "A road across the sea",
      "start": 222,
      "duration": 8,
      "image": "images/talk-beach-1.png",
      "background": "tyresea",
      "camera": "static",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Father",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Son",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "Wait. A road half a mile long, across open sea? In 332 BC? They didn't even have concrete!",
      "word_count": 18
    },
    {
      "id": "talk-beach-2",
      "speaker": "father",
      "section": "A road across the sea",
      "start": 230,
      "duration": 12,
      "image": "images/talk-beach-2.png",
      "background": "tyresea",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Father",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Son",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "Exactly. That's why the Tyrians watched from their walls like it was a comedy show. They just didn't realize who they were dealing with. Alexander didn't do detours.",
      "word_count": 28
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-08",
      "speaker": null,
      "sfx": [
        {
          "type": "hammer",
          "every": 0.55,
          "gain": 0.8
        }
      ],
      "section": "The engineers' war",
      "start": 242,
      "duration": 17,
      "image": "images/shot-08.png",
      "background": "tyresea",
      "camera": "static",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Worker",
          "expression": "determined",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Worker",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "Building the causeway",
      "narration": "So the work began. Alexander tore down the old town of Tyre on the mainland and dumped its stones into the sea. His men cut cedar trees in the mountains of Lebanon and drove them into the seabed.",
      "word_count": 38
    },
    {
      "id": "diades",
      "speaker": null,
      "sfx": [
        {
          "type": "hammer",
          "every": 0.7,
          "gain": 0.5
        }
      ],
      "section": "The engineers' war",
      "start": 259,
      "duration": 22,
      "image": "images/diades.png",
      "background": "tyresea",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Diades",
          "expression": "determined",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Alexander",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "Diades, chief engineer",
      "narration": "He put the right man in charge: Diades of Thessaly, his chief siege engineer and one of the best in the Greek world. And Alexander didn't watch from a tent. Ancient writers say he was on the site again and again, explaining the plan and rewarding the men who worked hardest.",
      "word_count": 51
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-09",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The engineers' war",
      "start": 281,
      "duration": 11,
      "image": "images/shot-09.png",
      "background": "tyresea",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": "About 200 ft wide",
      "narration": "Day after day, the causeway crept away from the beach. It was about two hundred feet wide, wide enough to march an army down.",
      "word_count": 24
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-10",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The engineers' war",
      "start": 292,
      "duration": 10,
      "image": "images/shot-10.png",
      "background": "tyrewall",
      "camera": "quick push in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Tyrian",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Tyrian",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "Up on the walls, the Tyrians stopped laughing. And as the causeway reached deeper water, their archers began shooting down at the workers.",
      "word_count": 23
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-11",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The engineers' war",
      "start": 302,
      "duration": 15,
      "image": "images/shot-11.png",
      "background": "tyresea",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": "Siege towers",
      "narration": "Alexander's answer: two huge wooden siege towers at the end of the causeway, taller than the walls, covered with raw hides so they wouldn't catch fire. Now his archers could shoot down at the Tyrians.",
      "word_count": 35
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-12",
      "speaker": null,
      "sfx": [
        {
          "type": "fire",
          "at": 0.45,
