        },
        {
          "name": "Soldier",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "walk"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "Red-hot sand",
      "narration": "The Tyrians grew desperate, and creative. They heated sand in bronze shields until it glowed, then poured it down on the attackers. It slipped under armor, and men tore off their gear just to get it out.",
      "word_count": 37
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-19",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Start again, bigger",
      "start": 441,
      "duration": 11,
      "image": "images/shot-19.png",
      "background": "tyresea",
      "camera": "static",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "Tyrian divers swam out and cut the anchor ropes of Alexander's ships, so he switched to iron chains. Every trick only slowed him down.",
      "word_count": 24
    },
    {
      "id": "cranes",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Start again, bigger",
      "start": 452,
      "duration": 23,
      "image": "images/cranes.png",
      "background": "tyresea",
      "camera": "static",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": "Cranes on ships",
      "narration": "The Tyrians had dumped huge boulders into the water at the foot of their walls, so no ship could get close. Alexander's answer: ships fitted with cranes that hauled the boulders out, one by one. Then he lashed ships together in pairs to carry battering rams, turning the sea itself into a siege platform.",
      "word_count": 54
    },
    {
      "id": "talk-boulders-1",
      "speaker": "son",
      "section": "Start again, bigger",
      "start": 475,
      "duration": 5,
      "image": "images/talk-boulders-1.png",
      "background": "tyresea",
      "camera": "static",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Father",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Son",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "Every time they blocked him, he just invented something new!",
      "word_count": 10
    },
    {
      "id": "talk-boulders-2",
      "speaker": "father",
      "section": "Start again, bigger",
      "start": 480,
      "duration": 12,
      "image": "images/talk-boulders-2.png",
      "background": "tyresea",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Father",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Son",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "That's the genius part, for me. Plenty of commanders are brave. Alexander was brave and creative, and he decided fast. He never let a problem sit for long.",
      "word_count": 28
    },
    {
      "id": "sortie",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Start again, bigger",
      "start": 492,
      "duration": 22,
      "image": "images/sortie.png",
      "background": "tyresea",
      "camera": "slow pan left",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": "The midday breakout",
      "narration": "The Tyrians tried one last surprise. At midday, while Alexander's sailors were resting, their ships slipped out of the harbor and attacked. Alexander saw it, grabbed every ship that was ready, and sailed straight around the island to cut them off. The breakout was crushed almost as soon as it began.",
      "word_count": 51
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-20",
      "speaker": null,
      "sfx": [
        {
          "type": "hammer",
          "at": 0.6,
          "every": 0.45,
          "until": 0.8,
          "gain": 0.9
        },
        {
          "type": "boom",
          "at": 0.8,
          "gain": 0.6
        }
      ],
      "section": "The fall of Tyre",
      "start": 514,
      "duration": 14,
      "image": "images/shot-20.png",
      "background": "tyresea",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": "July 332 BC",
      "narration": "After about seven months, the causeway finally reached the walls of Tyre. But the final blow came from the sea. Ships carrying battering rams broke open a section of the southern wall.",
      "word_count": 32
    },
    {
      "id": "assault",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The fall of Tyre",
      "start": 528,
      "duration": 15,
      "image": "images/assault.png",
      "background": "tyremap",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": "Attack everywhere at once",
      "narration": "Alexander's final plan was simple and relentless: hit everywhere at once. His ships attacked all around the island, so the defenders couldn't rush to one spot, while his fleets broke into both of Tyre's harbors.",
      "word_count": 35
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-21",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The fall of Tyre",
      "start": 543,
      "duration": 9,
      "image": "images/shot-21.png",
      "background": "tyrewall",
      "camera": "quick push in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Alexander",
          "expression": "determined",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Soldier",
          "expression": "determined",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Tyrian",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "walk"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "Alexander himself led the assault through the breach. After seven months of resistance, the city fell in a single day.",
      "word_count": 20
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-22",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The fall of Tyre",
      "start": 552,
      "duration": 15,
      "image": "images/shot-22.png",
      "background": "parchment",
      "camera": "static",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "The anger built up over seven months was terrible. According to the ancient historian Arrian, about eight thousand Tyrians fell in the fighting, and some thirty thousand people were sold into slavery.",
      "word_count": 32
    },
    {
      "id": "temple",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The fall of Tyre",
      "start": 567,
      "duration": 16,
      "image": "images/temple.png",
      "background": "temple",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Alexander",
          "expression": "closed",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "King of Tyre",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Tyrian",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "Temple of Heracles",
      "narration": "Afterwards, Alexander finally made his sacrifice at the temple of Heracles, the very thing the Tyrians had refused him seven months earlier. Those who had taken shelter inside the temple, including the king of Tyre, were spared.",
      "word_count": 37
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-23",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "A new map",
      "start": 583,
      "duration": 5,
      "image": "images/shot-23.png",
      "background": "tyremap",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": "Tyre, 332 BC",
      "narration": "And here's the craziest part. Alexander's causeway never went away.",
      "word_count": 10
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-24",
      "speaker": null,
      "sfx": [
        {
          "type": "whoosh",
          "at": 0
        }
      ],
      "section": "A new map",
      "start": 588,
